# Accessibility

Treat these as acceptance criteria, not polish. A story is not done if the screen is unusable with VoiceOver or at large text sizes.

- Every image, icon button, and control has a meaningful label. Decorative artwork is `.accessibilityHidden(true)`.
- Combine a cell's parts into one element so VoiceOver reads "Dune, rated 8.2, 2021" instead of three fragments: `.accessibilityElement(children: .combine)`.
- Speak values, not glyphs: `.accessibilityLabel("Rated 8.2 out of 10")` rather than a star string.
- Support Dynamic Type. No fixed font sizes and no fixed-height text containers; check the layout at `.accessibilityExtraExtraExtraLarge`.
- Tap targets are at least 44x44 points.
- Never convey state through color alone. Loading, failure, and selection are reflected in labels or traits.
- Sort and filter controls expose their current selection to VoiceOver, not just a checkmark glyph.
- Bookmark and favorite controls announce the action and the resulting state.
